        "type": "text",
        "text": "I have surveyed every location where an exclusivity or sole-supplier restraint could sit. Findings:\n\n- **§ 12.3 (p0044)** affirmatively preserves our freedom to engage any supplier and records that we made **no exclusivity** commitment.\n- **§ 7.2 (p0026)** disclose-and-match gate is a most-favoured-nation/right-to-match term (we may still engage another provider after disclosure) — addressed under the MFN rule, not double-flagged here.\n- **§ 2.1 (p0012)** take-or-pay volume floor belongs to the minimum-commitment rule; **§ 12.4 (second)** is a non-compete on our own products, not a purchasing restraint.\n- No \"exclusive\", \"sole supplier\", \"all of its requirements\", or \"shall not procure from any third party\" obligation binds us anywhere; the only \"exclusive\" hits are a non-exclusive licence grant to us, remedy/jurisdiction language, and Vendor-side IP ownership.\n\nNo exclusivity obligation binds the Customer, so the rule sits at the preferred position and no redline is warranted."
