          "rationale": "The Agreement imposes no exclusivity or sole-supplier obligation on us, which is the preferred position. Section 12.3 expressly preserves our freedom to engage any supplier and has Vendor acknowledge that we have made no exclusivity commitment; searches for \"exclusive\", \"sole\", \"requirements\", and \"procure … third party\" surface no purchasing restraint on Customer (the only \"exclusive\"/\"sole\" hits are the non-exclusive licence granted to us, remedy and jurisdiction language, and Vendor-side ownership/responsibility wording). Section 7.2's disclose-and-match gate before engaging another provider does not create exclusivity (we may still engage the other provider) and is a most-favoured-nation/right-to-match burden addressed under the MFN rule; Section 2.1's take-or-pay volume floor belongs to the minimum-commitment rule and the second Section 12.4 competition restraint is a non-compete, so none of them is flagged here to avoid double-counting the same commercial terms.",
